+## [Unreleased]: BLAKE2b chain identity
+
+### Added
+
+- Chain identity for the Bitcoin BLAKE2b chain (`doc/blake2b-chain-identity.md`):
+  the `chain_hash` carried in `init`, `open_channel`, gossip and BOLT 12 is the
+  id of block 961,640, the first BLAKE2b block, rather than Bitcoin's genesis,
+  which the chain shares; regtest, signet and testnet4 use a tagged hash of
+  their genesis. Invoices use the `lnblake`, `lnblakert`, `lntbsblake` and
+  `lntblake` prefixes, and a Bitcoin invoice (`lnbc...`) is refused.
+- Offers, invoice requests and invoices always name the chain: BOLT 12's
+  implicit chain stays Bitcoin mainnet, so an offer without `offer_chains`
+  is a Bitcoin offer and is not answered.
+- `init` messages that name no `networks` are dropped on this chain, since a
+  peer that sends none cannot be told from a Bitcoin node (LND never sent the
+  field). `--allow-peers-without-networks` keeps them, for testing.
+- A wallet stamped with Bitcoin's genesis by an earlier build of this fork is
+  restamped with the chain's `chain_hash` on the first start.
+
+### Changed
+
+- `when_lightning_became_cool` on mainnet is the activation height: no
+  channel on this chain is older.
+
